  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that N-Nornuciferine may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, N-Nornuciferine is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-((4-(Ethylamino)-6-methoxy-1,3,5-triazin-2-yl)amino)-2-methylpropiononitrile and (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one. These compounds are also predicted to target CD276 antigen. Additionally, N-Nornuciferine is linked to Guangsangon K, which is predicted to target CD276 antigen. The consistent presence of N-Nornuciferine as a target of DNA polymerase iota across multiple paths indicates a potential mechanism of action involving this enzyme. The evidence suggests that N-Nornuciferine may exert its effects through a pathway that involves DNA polymerase iota, which is then targeted by various compounds, ultimately leading to the inhibition of CD276 antigen. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the three paths, but the exact mechanism of interaction between N-Nornuciferine and CD276 antigen remains partially uncertain due to the lack of direct experimental validation.",
